// Test: a fragment SPREAD in an S2C root fragment is rejected, and rejected with
// advice that fits a spread.
//
// The spread here selects nothing but `id` — it is identity-only, so the shape is
// harmless in principle. It is still refused, because the walk checks selections
// one at a time and does not follow a spread into another fragment definition; it
// therefore cannot tell this apart from one that reads server data.
//
// The arm had no coverage at all before this fixture, which is how it came to
// share the generic diagnostic. That message offers `@UNSTABLE_key` as the fix, and a
// spread cannot be granted with `@UNSTABLE_key` — it would have read "Granting
// `UserIdentityFragment` asserts it is stable for the record's lifetime".
//
// The placeholder spread of a magic fragment does NOT reach here: it is replaced
// with the injected identity before `build_ir`, so a spread at this point is
// always one the author wrote.
//
// `@inline` on the spread is load-bearing, and finding that out is half of what
// this fixture records. A BARE spread never reaches the S2C rule — an earlier
// resolver validation demands `@inline` or `@relay(mask: false)` first — and
// `@relay(mask: false)` is inlined at `build_ir`, so the walk sees the contents
// rather than a spread. `@inline` is what survives as a `FragmentSpread` in the
// IR, which makes it the ONLY way to reach this arm.
//- FooQuery.js
graphql`query FooQuery @exec_time_resolvers {
  me {
    greeting
  }
}`

//- UserIdentity.js
graphql`fragment UserIdentityFragment on User @inline {
  id
}`

//- User_greeting.js
/**
 * @relayField User.greeting: RelayResolverValue
 * @rootFragment UserGreetingFragment
 */
graphql`fragment UserGreetingFragment on User {
  ...UserIdentityFragment
}`

//- relay.config.json
{
  "language": "flow",
  "jsModuleFormat": "haste",
  "schema": "schema.graphql",
  "schemaExtensions": ["schema-extensions"],
  "featureFlags": {
    "enable_exec_time_resolvers_directive": true
  }
}

//- schema.graphql
type Query {
  me: User
}

type User {
  id: ID!
  name: String
}

//- schema-extensions/extension.graphql
extend type User @UNSTABLE_key(fields: "name")
